From: CX3576-Z maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: rockusb: do not dequeue an idle IN request

The RockUSB function owns a single IN request.  Responses are submitted
either while that request is idle or from its completion callback, where the
gadget core has already removed it from the endpoint queue.  Calling
usb_ep_dequeue() in both paths therefore asks the UDC to cancel a request
which is not queued.  DWC3 reports this as:

  request ... was not queued to ep1in-bulk

Queue the idle request directly.  The bulk-only protocol does not issue the
next command until the current data/status phase completes, so there is no
active IN request to replace here.

---
 drivers/usb/gadget/f_rockusb.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_rockusb.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_rockusb.c
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/f_rockusb.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/f_rockusb.c
@@ -332,6 +332,5 @@ static int rockusb_tx_write(const char *buffer, unsigned int buffer_size)
 	in_req->length = buffer_size;
 	debug("Transferring 0x%x bytes\n", buffer_size);
-	usb_ep_dequeue(rockusb_func->in_ep, in_req);
 	ret = usb_ep_queue(rockusb_func->in_ep, in_req, 0);
 	if (ret)
 		printf("Error %d on queue\n", ret);
@@ -478,7 +477,6 @@ static void tx_handler_ul_image(struct usb_ep *ep, struct usb_request *req)
 	in_req->length = transfer_size;
 	in_req->complete = tx_handler_ul_image;
 	debug("Uploading 0x%x bytes\n", transfer_size);
-	usb_ep_dequeue(rockusb_func->in_ep, in_req);
 	ret = usb_ep_queue(rockusb_func->in_ep, in_req, 0);
 	if (ret)
 		printf("Error %d on queue\n", ret);
-- 
